 ## Overview
-Softmax-GS is a rendering method for 3D Gaussian Splatting that employs a softmax-based competition mechanism to handle overlapping Gaussians, aiming to provide order-invariance and smooth transitions at Gaussian boundaries [S1]. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting, which suffers from popping artifacts due to sorting dependencies, or StopThePop, which exhibits abrupt color changes, Softmax-GS produces flicker-free, smooth transitions by treating overlapping splats as a competitive blending process rather than a strict depth-sorted accumulation [S1]. It builds on [Tiled 2D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization](2061-tiled-2d-gaussian-splatting-rasterization.md) by replacing the standard alpha blending step with this differentiable, order-invariant softmax competition.
+Softmax-GS is a rendering method for 3D Gaussian Splatting that employs a softmax-based competition mechanism to handle overlapping Gaussians, aiming to provide order-invariance and smooth transitions at Gaussian boundaries [S1]. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting, which suffers from popping artifacts due to sorting dependencies, or StopThePop, which exhibits abrupt color changes, Softmax-GS produces flicker-free, smooth transitions by treating overlapping splats as a competitive blending process rather than a strict depth-sorted accumulation [S1]. It builds on [Tiled 2D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization](2061-tiled-2d-gaussian-splatting-rasterization.md) by replacing the standard alpha blending step with this differentiable, order-invariant softmax competition [S1].
 
